vapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"21c2aa0705a0600102dad6301c0fc6d6cf62b14012992446844f24fa8d716c35","event_uuid":"6183a892-221c-45b4-9150-3e8eda29fe1c","position":{"commit_sha":"b17cb516019f6fc477a200b8f3b3d530484ce6ca","position":"1793816877263458001-6183a892-221c-45b4-9150-3e8eda29fe1c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause confirmed by 2-clone reproduction: rebuild_snapshot_under_lock placed the rebuilt SNAPSHOT at hlc.next_tick (repair clock); fsck does not fetch, so a tag written on clone B 24 s before the repair merged in before the SNAPSHOT, uncited (ORPHAN_EVENT). Fix reuses compact_txn._snapshot_timestamp with the configured horizon and no young events; anchor is the newest RAW source (not a prior clock-placed SNAPSHOT). Unreadable config aborts before mutation. Tests: 3 new positive-horizon/abort tests fail before (3 failed, 5 passed) and pass after (8 passed); 688 passed, 2 skipped across compact/fsck/fold/rebuild/snapshot modules; make lint and make typecheck exit 0; rebuild_snapshot_under_lock complexity unchanged at 12. Gerrit change 3308.","timestamp":1793814254232854001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793790241584902001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9a38bf52-0224-4c17-9f39-5eab20a8f429","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2977-df28-8e9f-4a50"},{"link_uuid":"636ecb05-c893-4af1-82cf-6e2776011716","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f28c-baa3-d8a2-4383"},{"link_uuid":"6183a892-221c-45b4-9150-3e8eda29fe1c","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"2977-df28-8e9f-4a50"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`compact_rebuild.rebuild_snapshot_under_lock` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py:143`, the `rebar store fsck --repair-snapshots` path via `fsck_restore.rebuild_with_restore` -> `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log`, and the ensure sweep via `src/rebar/_store/snapshot_ensures.py:76`) stamps its rebuilt SNAPSHOT with `hlc.next_tick(tracker, ticket_id)`, the repairing host's clock. The rebuild absorbs every raw event it has on disk, but an event another clone wrote after the newest local event and before the repair, not yet fetched (fsck does not fetch), later merges in with a timestamp before that SNAPSHOT and is not cited by it. fsck then reports it as `ORPHAN_EVENT` (`fsck_repair.is_snapshot_orphan`) and replay drops its effect. This is the placement defect bug stormproof-stormy-toad fixed for the fold (Gerrit 3301, `dc6300ce801`) through `compact_txn._snapshot_timestamp` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:297`).\n\nIt matters now: operator task respirable-trapezial-ekaltadeta will run `fsck --repair-snapshots` on ticket 77b6-868f, which takes this path.\n\n## Approach\n\nReuse the fold's single placement rule instead of writing a second one. A rebuild is a full fold with no young live events, so call `_snapshot_timestamp(tracker, ticket_id, old=<raw sources>, young=[], now=hlc.physical_now(), horizon=<configured horizon>)`:\n\n- `horizon` is `config.compose_config(None).compact.COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS` (default 30 min, `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:247`), read the same way `compact.py:82` and `compact_trigger.py:89` read it. A positive horizon gives fold-boundary placement (newest absorbed event's timestamp + 1); `horizon <= 0` (archive stores, the offline test suite's default via `tests/conftest.py:664`) keeps clock placement, exactly as the fold does. A `config.ConfigError` aborts the rebuild with a warning and returns False, matching the rebuild's existing fail-closed exits.\n- `old` is the raw (non-SNAPSHOT) sources, active and `*.retired`, which `_partition_rebuild_sources` already lists as `compact_plan.Candidate`s with parsed timestamps. With `young=[]`, `_snapshot_timestamp` never returns None.\n- Anchor for an already-compacted ticket: the newest raw event in the rebuilt set, NOT the prior SNAPSHOT. A prior SNAPSHOT placed at a clock (before 3301) sits after every raw event; anchoring on it would leave the gap between the newest raw event and that clock reading, where an unfetched remote event lands as an orphan again. The prior SNAPSHOT is retired by the rebuild, so a new SNAPSHOT sorting before it has no effect on replay. `_partition_rebuild_sources` already separates snapshots from raw sources, so the anchor follows from passing only raw sources.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py`: `_partition_rebuild_sources` returns the raw `Candidate`s (callers derive paths from them); a small helper reads the horizon and calls `compact_txn._snapshot_timestamp`; `rebuild_snapshot_under_lock` uses it in place of `hlc.next_tick`. File stays under 250 lines; `rebuild_snapshot_under_lock` stays under the complexity threshold of 15 (currently 12).\n- `tests/integration/test_fold_cross_clone_horizon.py`: a 2-clone rebuild test beside the existing fold test, reusing its helpers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fold_horizon_placement.py`: a pinned-clock unit test of the rebuild anchor.\n\nNo `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` change.\n\n## Testing\n\nBoth new tests are written first and must fail on the unfixed tree.\n\n- Integration (2 clones, real child processes, pinned physical clocks via `_child_hooks.child_env(hlc_now=...)`, env via `_subprocess_env.subprocess_env`, no autouse fixtures): clone A creates and comments; clone B writes a COMMENT that A folds past at horizon 0 (clock placement), so after A merges it A holds an auto-recoverable `ORPHAN_EVENT`. B then tags the ticket 24 s before A runs `store fsck --repair-snapshots` with `REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS` = 30 min and without fetching. A then merges B's tag. Assert: the tag file sorts after A's rebuilt SNAPSHOT, `show` on A includes the tag, and `store fsck --output json` reports no `orphan_event` for the ticket.\n- Unit (pinned `hlc._clock`): a compacted ticket whose prior SNAPSHOT sits at a later clock than its newest raw event; with a positive horizon, the rebuilt SNAPSHOT's timestamp equals the newest raw source's timestamp + 1, which is below the prior SNAPSHOT's. With horizon 0 it is the clock (`hlc.next_tick`), unchanged.\n- Regression: the compaction, fsck and fold test modules (`tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py`, `tests/unit/test_fold_horizon_placement.py`, `tests/integration/test_fold_cross_clone_horizon.py`, `tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck*.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_rebuild_counter_b2bb.py`, and other `-k \"compact or fsck or fold or rebuild\"` selections), then `make lint` and `make typecheck` with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A 2-clone test in `tests/integration/test_fold_cross_clone_horizon.py` shows an event written on clone B before a `store fsck --repair-snapshots` on clone A replays on A after the merge, and `store fsck --output json` on A reports no `orphan_event` for the ticket; the test fails on the unfixed tree and passes after the change.\n- [x] A unit test in `tests/unit/test_fold_horizon_placement.py` shows that, under a positive horizon, a rebuild of an already-compacted ticket places its SNAPSHOT at the newest raw source's timestamp + 1, and under horizon 0 at the clock; it fails on the unfixed tree for the positive-horizon case.\n- [x] `rebuild_snapshot_under_lock` obtains its timestamp from `compact_txn._snapshot_timestamp`; `hlc.next_tick` no longer appears in `src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py` (`grep -c next_tick` prints 0).\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0 in the worktree, and every `src/rebar` file stays at or under 800 lines.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py","reason":"place the rebuilt SNAPSHOT through compact_txn._snapshot_timestamp"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_fold_cross_clone_horizon.py","reason":"2-clone repair-snapshots reproduction"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fold_horizon_placement.py","reason":"pinned-clock rebuild anchor test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","f28c-baa3-d8a2-4383"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5973f727-db6c-4af8-b9df-62d4ca9a7e7e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["tracker","compaction"],"ticket_id":"e1dd-29e9-d123-47fc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Snapshot rebuild places SNAPSHOT at repair clock, orphaning unfetched events","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ef2315d0-c2da-4cdf-995f-e64398db4ef0","949f96ac-79d7-4b51-a9df-a36ba2c38c27","849c0732-72c9-4024-b747-e057ddc942d3","170e9c79-ea64-4d59-a309-30df50fa7f38","a47b6be0-41a7-4411-8127-d894b1de32b0","0d3b268e-cdfd-489c-877b-211cf97d26f2","636ecb05-c893-4af1-82cf-6e2776011716","5a0797a3-aa52-4e70-afbb-1fee01216410","ec5f2e05-ee8b-4a5f-8d25-68d3b2639653","5973f727-db6c-4af8-b9df-62d4ca9a7e7e","685d1695-2bb7-4e6b-add2-6117370d659e","6183a892-221c-45b4-9150-3e8eda29fe1c"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793816877263458002,"uuid":"2cdc5c49-ae12-4bc3-b99c-68d5a5a8efc8"}